#!/bin/sh
cat <<'TXT'
Созвездие / Constellation

Installing erases one whole disk and gives you:
  * an OpenZFS root with boot environments: updates go into a copy of the system
    (sudo constellation-be upgrade), so a bad update never touches the one you are using
  * ZFSBootMenu to boot any boot environment or snapshot
  * niri and the Caelestia shell, the birthDate-free systemd, zram instead of swap
  * the Russian kit (constellation-russian; downloads with constellation-content)

1. Connect to the internet (Ethernet works by itself). For Wi-Fi:
       iwctl station wlan0 scan
       iwctl station wlan0 get-networks
       iwctl station wlan0 connect "Network name"
2. Check the computer started in UEFI mode:  ls /sys/firmware/efi
3. Install:  constellation-install
   Rehearse first, changing nothing:  constellation-install --dry-run
TXT
